csq-socks.exe includes gVisor's netstack (gvisor.dev/gvisor, Apache License 2.0, Copyright The gVisor Authors) with
one change, source/gvisor-tcp-undo.patch: its TCP undoes the window cut of a recovery it finds spurious, so packets the
csqtt workers deliver out of order no longer hold the upload of `csq-socks up` near 3 Mbit/s.
LICENSE-csq-socks-exe.txt (in the Windows archive) carries the licences of everything compiled into csq-socks.exe:
Go (BSD-3-Clause, with its patent grant), gVisor and google/btree (Apache License 2.0), wireguard-go, wireguard-windows
and the wintun Go package (MIT), golang.org/x/net, x/sys and x/time (BSD-3-Clause).

